You'll have to remove
your sunglasses for this.

255
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:55,690
Sure.

256
00:17:58,860 --> 00:18:00,480
ID verified. Proceed.

257
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:06,985
Security's awfully tight here.

258
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:09,597
You'd think the middle
of the ocean was safe.

259
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:13,220
Actually, we're required to
run full body checks on guests.

260
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:18,292
But you've gone through three metal
and explosives detectors already, so...

261
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:43,700
Welcome to Wrath, Doctor.

262
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:46,417
Ki-Kuoka.

263
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,260
Sorry, Lieutenant Colonel.

264
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:50,780
You look comfy.

265
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,057
Where's your uniform?

266
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:54,787
Um, sir, I'll be on the
comms if you need me.

267
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:59,817
I've been stuck out here in the middle
of the ocean for about a month now.

268
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:03,640
I can't always be in a uniform,
or a suit for that matter.

269
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:08,642
I can't begin to tell you how happy
I am to finally have you here.

270
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:12,197
I was starting to worry my
persistence scared you away.

271
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:15,751
Just because I'm here doesn't
mean I've agreed to anything.

272
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:19,440
Fair enough.

273
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:21,744
But before you decide anything,

274
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:26,717
you should know you're one of three people
whose skills are crucial to this project.

275
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:28,780
And now, you're all here.

276
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:31,201
Congratulations.

277
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:33,188
Well, well, look who it is.

278
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:36,224
Don't tell me he roped
you in on this too, Higa.

279
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:38,077
What do you think?

280
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,160
Of course he did.

281
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:41,517
Honestly, I'm stoked to be here.

282
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:44,960
I'm carrying on the legacy
of Shigemura Lab. I swear.

283
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:47,478
You haven't changed a bit, have you?

284
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:50,260
Well, who's the third
person you mentioned?

285
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:53,852
Unfortunately, I can't introduce you now.

286
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:55,200
But don't worry.

287
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:56,497
In a few days, I'll show...

288
00:19:56,580 --> 00:19:57,410
Mr.

289
00:19:57,493 --> 00:19:59,380
Kikoka, you'll take us to him.

290
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:00,730
Now.

291
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:05,557
Asuna, I...

292
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:07,200
What are you doing here?

293
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:10,160
She sent me an interesting email.

294
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:18,880
An organization called Wrath is developing
a machine called the Soul Translator.

295
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:20,860
It's based on the Medicuboid,

296
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:24,452
the medical full-dive rig you
designed the technology for.

297
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:29,677
Kazuto Kirigaya was testing
this new machine but

298
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:32,584
he disappeared and I need
your help to find him.

299
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:37,857
Kazuto Kirigaya I was
in the old Sao server

300
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:40,960
and I met Kayaba's digital ghost there.

301
00:20:42,340 --> 00:20:47,457
We spoke he gave me a
program called the Seed do

302
00:20:47,540 --> 00:20:50,599
you know it if you do I'd
like to get your thoughts.

303
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:59,069
If you hate him for what he did, then
just delete it and forget all about it.

304
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:02,380
It's okay, really. End it.

305
00:21:02,580 --> 00:21:06,227
But if there's still a part of
you that sees VR's potential...

306
00:21:08,420 --> 00:21:09,877
After Kirito disappeared,

307
00:21:09,960 --> 00:21:13,725
I went through his contacts and
that's where I found your email.

308
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:18,449
If you know anything about Wrath, anything
at all, it could help me find him.

309
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:23,380
You're my last hope, Dr.
Kojiro. Help me. Please.

310
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:25,230
Sorry.

311
00:21:25,313 --> 00:21:26,420
Did we surprise you?

312
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:30,437
Are you having second thoughts now about
inviting me to be on your project, Mr.

313
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:31,350
Kikwoka?

314
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:34,277
Apparently our security
wasn't thorough enough.

315
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:37,277
I know we have your assistant's
photo from the university.

316
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:40,200
They should have run a
proper check. They did.

317
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:44,177
On our way in, they scanned my
face quite a few times, in fact.

318
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:46,717
But I had her assistant's
photo in the school's

319
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:49,153
database switched with mine a while ago.

320
00:21:50,040 --> 00:21:53,922
I happen to know someone who's
great at busting through firewalls.

321
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:59,026
Right now, the real Mayumi is probably
on a beach somewhere, working on her tan.

322
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:04,060
Take me to Kirito!

323
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:29,280
must be Alice to you
